      "problem": "Determine the range of the function $f(x)=2{log}_{5}⁡(2x-1)+1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of the function $y={log}_{5}⁡(x)$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nHorizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range of a logarithmic function.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$",
